From d481afbe804dfd3a8ce252ca847eeff7a767730a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kudbee <twd4lifez@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:34:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(infra): add upcloud-ssh governed execution substrate
 (#282)

Adds a third explicit substrate to thinkbox/governed_job_execution.py, so
governed POST /api/v1/run can execute a bounded command on the UpCloud
worker. UpCloudSSHExecutionAdapter uses the same receipt/artifact/checkpoint
contract as LocalExecutionAdapter and delegates the remote call to the
existing SSHCloudExecutionProvider. It is configured from the env vars that
UpCloudConfig already reads (UPCLOUD_SERVER_IP / UPCLOUD_SSH_USER /
UPCLOUD_SSH_KEY_PATH; the key path only). It fails closed with
remote_not_configured and never falls back to local (H09 extended).
Substrate lists stay consistent across lifecycle_harden/reclaim/resume.

Live proof on the real backend.main:app (in-process, real governance, no
hooks): POST /api/v1/run {execution_substrate: upcloud-ssh,
exec_command: hostname} -> admitted -> SSH root@209.50.51.174 ->
"kudbee-hermes-worker-02", exit 0. It produced a hash-verified artifact,
checkpoint, receipt (GET 200) and a completed ThinkJobEntry with
dashboard events, in 1.92s end to end.

Tests: 13 unit + 3 e2e. Regression is 271/271 locally. CI does not run
(GitHub billing issue).

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
